<title>GERMANY: SKW Trostberg 1996 income rises.</title>
<headline>SKW Trostberg 1996 income rises.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>German speciality chemicals group SKW Trostberg AG said on Wednesday that its 1996 group income from ordinary activities rose to 247.1 million marks ($147.1 million) from 221.6 million previously.</p>
<p>The company's profit per share for the year according the DVFA accounting rules rose to 2.25 marks versus 2.03 marks in the previous year.</p>
<p>The firm also said its first quarter profits for 1997 were well above those made in the same period a year earlier.</p>
<p>SKW said sales for the whole of this year would be more than five billion marks and added that 1997 profits would grow at a faster pace than in 1996. ($ = 1.679 German Marks)</p>
